{
    "debug mode": 0,
    "// 3-CAMERA MULTI-VIEW //": "Mirrors all_cams_dec18: concat fusion, dilation 2 - the original multi-view architecture. 3-CAMERA multi-view model for the OLD RIG. 'number of cameras': 3 makes the preprocessor turn every labelled frame into one sample per 3-of-4 camera subset (C(4,3) = 4 subsets, 1608 samples), so the model sees four camera combinations instead of memorising one. That also means a camera SLOT is not tied to one physical camera, which is what makes 'concat' fusion usable here at all. Epochs are 40 rather than 100 because each epoch already covers 4x the samples. NOTE: trained on the 4-camera rig's labelled frames minus one camera - a proxy for the old rig, not the real thing. If 2D quality on real 3-camera movies is poor, the fix is labelled frames from the old rig.",
